userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the shared styled confirmation service and a single app-level dialog host.

**Motivation** — The browser can suppress that dialog, it says nothing about what happens, and it does not match the styled Archive dialog on threads.

**Approach** — New `apps/web/composables/useConfirm.ts` (auto-imported). It has no precedent in the app, so here is a worked skeleton:

```ts
import { computed, shallowRef } from 'vue'

export interface ConfirmOptions { title: string; body?: string; confirmLabel?: string; destructive?: boolean }
interface Pending { options: ConfirmOptions; resolve: (ok: boolean) => void }

// One dialog per tab. Client-only: confirm() is called from event handlers, never during setup or SSR.
const pending = shallowRef<Pending | null>(null)

export function useConfirm() {
  function confirm(options: ConfirmOptions): Promise<boolean> {
    pending.value?.resolve(false)
    return new Promise<boolean>((resolve) => { pending.value = { options, resolve } })
  }
  function settle(ok: boolean): void {
    const current = pending.value
    if (!current) return
    pending.value = null
    current.resolve(ok)
  }
  return { confirm, settle, current: computed(() => pending.value?.options ?? null) }
}
```

New `apps/web/components/ConfirmDialogHost.vue`. It reads `useConfirm().current` and renders, only while `current` is non-null, a `Dialog` (open) with `DialogContent data-testid="confirm-dialog"` containing:
- `DialogTitle` = `title`;
- a muted paragraph `data-testid="confirm-dialog-body"` = `body`, shown only when `body` is set;
- `DialogFooter` with Cancel (`data-testid="confirm-dialog-cancel"`, `variant="outline"`, `t('common.cancel')`) and Confirm (`data-testid="confirm-dialog-confirm"`, text `confirmLabel ?? t('common.confirm')`, `variant="destructive"` when `destructive` is true and `"default"` otherwise).

Confirm calls `settle(true)`. Cancel, and the `Dialog` emitting `update:open` with `false` (Escape, overlay), call `settle(false)`.

`apps/web/app.vue`.
- Baseline: `NuxtLayout` > `NuxtPage`, then `Toaster`.
- Target: the same, plus one `<ConfirmDialogHost />` after `Toaster`.

Modify `apps/web/tests/helpers/mount-sfc.ts` — add `useConfirm` to `NUXT_AUTO_IMPORTS`, and to `AUTO_IMPORT_DEFAULTS` as `() => ({ confirm: async () => true, settle: () => undefined, current: { value: null } })`, so every existing mount of a component that now calls `useConfirm` still runs. A spec that tests the dialog overrides it through `globals`.

`useConfirm` holds module state, so every spec in this story settles any pending request in an `afterEach` (or isolates the module per test), and no test depends on another's leftover request. Add `tests/composables/useConfirm.spec.ts` for AC-1 to AC-4 and `tests/components/confirm-dialog-host.spec.ts` for AC-5 to AC-13, using the existing Dialog stubs and real shared state for host settlement tests.

**Scope** — In: the shared composable, host, app mount and mount-harness integration. Out: adopting the service in comment deletion (US-003), ticket deletion (US-004), or the remaining native-confirm sites deferred to `e2e-1121-confirm-dialogs`; calling confirm during setup or SSR.

**Interface** — `ConfirmOptions`, `Pending`, `confirm(options: ConfirmOptions): Promise<boolean>`, `settle(ok: boolean): void`, and `current: computed(() => pending.value?.options ?? null)` are defined verbatim in the skeleton above.
